<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<RecordType xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT and must stay that way. A comment
        placed ABOVE <RecordType> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with the misleading
        error "unable to find matching parent xml file". The <description> below is deliberately
        short because RecordType.description is capped at 255 CHARACTERS - a cap this programme
        has now breached FIVE times, every one caught only by measuring. Long rationale goes
        here, where nothing is sent to the Metadata API and length is unlimited.

        THE BUY-SIDE PSA. This is the shape that exists today: DPEG is the buyer, the paper
        comes from the seller's counsel, and Ball_In_Court__c 'Seller' correctly names the
        counterparty. Parented by Opportunity__c; Disposition__c stays blank.

        ⚠ BOTH RECORD TYPES EXPOSE THE SAME FOUR Negotiation_Status__c VALUES, AND THAT IS THE
        POINT - IT IS NOT AN OVERSIGHT TO BE "FIXED" LATER. Initial Draft -> Revised -> Ready
        for Execution -> Executed are ALREADY exactly the four states the client document names
        for the sell-side PSA, so unlike LOI__c and NDA__c there is no second vocabulary to
        carry. Contract_Review__c therefore needs NO record-type-aware stage map in
        RecordStageAdvanceService - it keeps ONE map serving both types. Anyone adding a
        disposition-only status here should re-read that: it would turn a one-map object into a
        two-map object and drag the Apex change back into scope.

        WHAT THE TWO TYPES ACTUALLY DIFFER ON is exactly two things: the counterparty token in
        Ball_In_Court__c (Seller here, Buyer on Disposition_PSA) and which parent lookup is
        populated. That is the whole delta.

        EVERY PICKLIST ON THE OBJECT IS LISTED HERE, INCLUDING ONES THIS CHANGE DOES NOT ALTER.
        A record type file that OMITS a picklist silently drops ALL of that picklist's values
        for the type - the field then offers nothing. Contract_Review__c has exactly THREE
        picklists: Ball_In_Court__c, Negotiation_Status__c and Stage__c. The fields/ directory
        was walked field by field to establish that, and the walk corrected the design document,
        which also named Asset_Type__c and Deal_Type__c - both are formula TEXT fields (they
        cross-object-read Opportunity__r), not picklists, and a picklistValues block naming
        either would be invalid.

        🔴 Stage__c IS A DERIVED FIELD. Contract_Review_Stage_Sync recomputes it from
        Negotiation_Status__c on every save, and a direct write to it COMMITS AND IS SILENTLY
        DISCARDED - measured org behaviour, not theory. It is listed here only so its values do
        not vanish from the type. Nothing in 3C writes it, and nothing added later should.

        THE THREE isActive=false LEGACY Stage__c VALUES ARE DELIBERATELY OMITTED
        ('Contract Execution (Signed)', 'Contract Negotiation', 'Prepare'). An inactive value is
        unselectable org-wide, so listing it grants nothing, while naming a value the platform
        does not consider live risks the exact "picklist value does not exist" rejection that
        cost 3A a two-phase deploy. ⚠ NO IN-REPO PRECEDENT EXISTS EITHER WAY - a sweep of every
        recordType file found none that references a field carrying inactive values, so this is
        the first case and it is a DEPLOY GATE, not a settled pattern. If a legacy value is ever
        reactivated it must be added here explicitly.

        NO URL-ENCODING IS NEEDED IN THIS FILE, which is worth stating because it is the
        exception. Inside a RecordType a picklist fullName must be URL-encoded (the repo
        precedent is Prepare%2FReview on LOI__c and Dead%2FPass in Opportunity's business
        processes). Every value listed here contains only letters and spaces - spaces are NOT
        encoded - so all fullNames are literal. The one value that would have needed it,
        'Contract Execution (Signed)', is inactive and omitted.

        NO <businessProcess> ELEMENT. That element applies to Opportunity, Case, Lead and
        Solution only; Contract_Review__c is a custom object.

        🔴 HANDOFF - APEX, NOT BUILT HERE (D16.3, the third and last of the three).
        OpportunityReviewService:100 inserts Contract_Review__c and stamps NO record type.
        Left alone, every auto-created ACQUISITION PSA lands on Master - one deal at a time,
        forever, silently - which is damage to a working flow caused by adding record types to
        an object whose creator predates them. The class already carries the pattern for NDA__c
        and LOI__c: a describe resolved ONCE per invocation (zero SOQL), an isAvailable() guard,
        and a test that re-reads RecordTypeId FROM THE DATABASE and fails unconditionally. ⚠ The
        guard question must be RE-ARGUED for this insert rather than inherited: the NDA guard
        exists because ensureNda runs on EVERY Opportunity insert including
        Database.convertLead, so an unguarded stamp would break lead conversion org-wide before
        gate T-A1 runs. This insert fires only on entry to the PSA stage, which is a narrower
        blast radius - but it is still pre-gate-reachable, so the guarded shape is the
        conservative match.
    -->
    <fullName>Acquisition_PSA</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>The buy-side PSA. DPEG is the buyer, so the counterparty is the Seller and Ball In Court reads Us / Seller. Parented by Opportunity; the Disposition lookup stays blank. Same four Negotiation Status values as the disposition type.</description>
    <label>Acquisition PSA</label>
    <picklistValues>
        <picklist>Ball_In_Court__c</picklist>
        <values>
            <fullName>Us</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Seller</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
    </picklistValues>
    <picklistValues>
        <picklist>Negotiation_Status__c</picklist>
        <values>
            <fullName>Initial Draft</fullName>
            <default>true</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Revised</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Ready for Execution</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Executed</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
    </picklistValues>
    <picklistValues>
        <picklist>Stage__c</picklist>
        <values>
            <fullName>PSA Drafting</fullName>
            <default>true</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Review</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Contract Execution</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
    </picklistValues>
</RecordType>
